---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SEO from '@components/SEO.astro';

const lastUpdated = '15 January 2025';

const seoData = {
  title: 'Terms of Service — Tenderpreneur',
  description:
    'Tenderpreneur terms of service. Read our terms for using the platform, subscription and payment terms, and acceptable use policy.',
  canonical: 'https://tenderpreneur.co.za/terms',
  ogImage: 'https://tenderpreneur.co.za/og-default.png',
};
---

<BaseLayout>
  <SEO slot="head" {...seoData} />

  <!-- Page Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-navy-900 to-civic-800 py-16 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb mb-6">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-sky-300">
          <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true">›</li>
          <li aria-current="page" class="text-white">Terms of Service</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-white">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sky-300">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Content -->
  <section class="bg-white py-16 dark:bg-navy-950">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="prose prose-tp mx-auto">

        <p class="lead">
          By accessing or using Tenderpreneur (tenderpreneur.co.za and app.tenderpreneur.co.za),
          you agree to these Terms of Service. Please read them carefully. If you do not agree,
          do not use the platform.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who these terms apply to</h2>
        <p>
          These terms apply to all users of Tenderpreneur, including visitors, free-tier users,
          Professional subscribers, and Enterprise clients. "Tenderpreneur" means Tenderpreneur
          (Pty) Ltd, a company registered in South Africa.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What Tenderpreneur provides</h2>
        <p>
          Tenderpreneur provides a government tender intelligence platform that aggregates publicly
          available tender information, publishes procurement guidance, and offers AI-assisted
          tools to help South African businesses navigate government procurement. Tenderpreneur
          is an information service, not a procurement agent. We do not submit tenders on your
          behalf, provide legal advice, or guarantee procurement outcomes.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Account registration</h2>
        <p>
          To access most features you must create an account. You agree to provide accurate
          information, keep your login credentials secure, and notify us immediately if you
          suspect unauthorised access. You are responsible for all activity under your account.
          You must be 18 or older to register.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Subscription plans and payment</h2>

        <h3>Free plan</h3>
        <p>
          The Free plan provides access to the PFMA knowledge base, SBD form library, and
          compliance checklist at no cost. We may modify Free plan features at any time with
          30 days' notice.
        </p>

        <h3>Professional plan</h3>
        <p>
          The Professional plan is billed monthly at R299 (inclusive of VAT) via PayFast.
          Your subscription renews automatically each month. You authorise Tenderpreneur to
          charge your nominated payment method on the same day each month.
        </p>

        <h3>Enterprise plan</h3>
        <p>
          Enterprise pricing is agreed by contract. Payment terms are set out in the individual
          enterprise agreement.
        </p>

        <h3>Cancellation</h3>
        <p>
          You may cancel your Professional subscription at any time from your account settings.
          Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. We do not issue
          pro-rata refunds for unused days unless required by the Consumer Protection Act 68 of
          2008 or another applicable South African law.
        </p>

        <h3>Price changes</h3>
        <p>
          We may change subscription pricing with 30 days' written notice. If you do not accept
          the new price, you may cancel before the change takes effect.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Scrape, crawl, or systematically download Tenderpreneur content without written permission</li>
          <li>Resell, sublicense, or redistribute Tenderpreneur data to third parties</li>
          <li>Use the platform to submit fraudulent tenders or engage in fronting under the B-BBEE Act</li>
          <li>Attempt to circumvent security controls or access other users' data</li>
          <li>Use the AI assistant to generate false compliance documents</li>
          <li>Violate any South African law including the PFMA, B-BBEE Act, or POPIA</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Tenderpreneur content — including PFMA guides, blog posts, AI assistant responses, and
          platform design — is protected by copyright. You may use it for your own procurement
          purposes but may not reproduce or republish it without permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tender notices displayed on Tenderpreneur originate from public procurement portals
          operated by the South African government. They remain in the public domain.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          Tenderpreneur provides information for general guidance only. Our PFMA content, AI
          assistant responses, and compliance tools do not constitute legal advice. Procurement
          regulations change frequently. Always verify critical compliance requirements against
          the current legislation and consult a qualified procurement professional for complex
          matters.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tenderpreneur aggregates tender data from third-party government portals. We strive
          for accuracy but cannot guarantee that all tenders are complete, current, or error-free.
          Always verify tender details on the originating portal before bidding.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by South African law, Tenderpreneur's liability for
          any claim arising from your use of the platform is limited to the total subscription
          fees you paid in the 12 months preceding the claim. We are not liable for lost business,
          tender disqualifications, or procurement decisions made in reliance on our platform.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of South Africa. Disputes will
          be resolved in the courts of South Africa, with Cape Town as the agreed jurisdiction.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. We will notify users by email at least
          14 days before material changes take effect. Continued use of Tenderpreneur after the
          effective date constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:legal@tenderpreneur.co.za">legal@tenderpreneur.co.za</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
